      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HIGHLAND KITTY (6) has returned in good order and is desperate to break through. Strips rock-hard fit and gets in light again with another 3kg claimer engaged. Draws to get all the favours and gets another great chance to shed the tag. JOSEPHINE OF TUFFY (7) is the clear danger on consistency, with six placings from 11 starts and a reliable record at this venue. She looks the one they'll need to reel in. FLIRTING WITH FIRE (5) has a smaller winning case but her fourth behind Crunch Time had merit after racing wide without cover, while PANZER READY (3) improved into fourth at Gatton and can be competitive if he handles 1910m at the first attempt. O'EXPLOSIVE (2) is another that finds the maiden win elusive, and while he's currently in poor touch, he has placed at both attempts over this track and trip. That's not nothing.",
